//? Title: Edmonds–Karp: Actual Shortest Paths, Cancellations and Cut Witnesses
//? Subtitle: From one bottleneck to the original CLRS network and exact BFS work
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a directed network with capacity limits, we want to send as much
flow as possible from a source to a sink while conserving flow elsewhere.
An earlier routing decision may need to be undone to make room for a
better one. Edmonds–Karp repeatedly finds a shortest residual path and
pushes its bottleneck. We inspect a tiny bottleneck and an actual reverse
cancellation, preserve the original six-vertex example, and check exact
search counts against a blocking-flow method. Owned execution evidence,
cut certificates and explicit numerical limits make the results checkable.
)

\toc

> Start with one bottleneck and a matching cut

Take s=0, an intermediate vertex 1 and t=2, with capacities three
and two along the chain. A first BFS finds 0→1→2. Its bottleneck
is min(3,2)=2: pushing two leaves residual capacities one and zero.
The final BFS still reaches vertex 1, but cannot reach the sink.
Thus S={0,1}, and its only outgoing capacity is two. Flow and cut agree.

The native figure uses the actual result. Edge labels are input
identity: flow/capacity; green nodes belong to the supplied source side,
and red edges cross that cut. The drawing API preserves input identities
and supports parallel, antiparallel and self edges as well.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/edmonds_karp_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::FlowNetwork g{3,{{0,1,3},{1,2,2}},0,2};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::edmonds_karp_trace(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink);
  const auto c=dm::algorithms::max_flow_certificate(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink,t.result);
  std::print("Tiny: flow {}; searches {}; adjacency inspections {}; captured entries {}.\n",t.result.max_flow,t.work.bfs_calls,t.work.bfs_arc_inspections,t.captured_entries);
  std::print("Feasible {}; optimal with zero tolerance {}; cut capacity {}; duality gap {}.\n\n",c.feasible,c.optimal_within_tolerance,c.cut_capacity,c.duality_gap);
  std::print("| search | vertex | residual distance | parent oriented arc id |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- |\n");
  const auto none=std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max();
  for(std::size_t k=0;k<t.searches.size();++k)for(std::size_t v=0;v<g.vertex_count;++v){const auto& b=t.searches[k];
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,v,b.levels[v]==g.vertex_count?std::string("unreachable"):std::to_string(b.levels[v]),b.parents[v]==none?std::string("none"):std::to_string(b.parents[v]));}
  std::print("\n| actual path edge | used residual before | used residual after | cancellation before | cancellation after |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& a:t.augmentations.at(0).path)std::print("| e{}: {} to {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",a.input_edge,a.from,a.to,a.residual_before,a.residual_after,a.paired_before,a.paired_after);
  auto d=dm::algorithms::plot_max_flow(g,t.result,{{0,0},{5,0},{10,0}});
  d.text({5,2},"One bottleneck push: min(3,2) = 2",25).text({5,-1.8},"Red edge leaves the final source side S = {0,1}",20).save_svg("build/edmonds_karp_tiny.svg");
}
