> Why shortest paths bound the work

After an augmentation, residual source distances cannot decrease. Any
newly positive arc is a reverse of an arc used on the shortest path;
it points from level d+1 back to level d. Such an arc cannot create a
shorter source path. Induction along a hypothetical first shortened path
makes this contradiction precise. Complete BFS records let us inspect
all distances, including vertices that become unreachable.

Each augmentation saturates at least one oriented residual arc (u,v).
For that same arc to be saturated again, it must first regain capacity
through reverse use. Between those events, its tail distance increases
by at least two. A vertex has fewer than V finite distance levels, so
an oriented arc can be charged O(V) times. Summing over the 2E residual
arcs gives O(VE) augmentations, independently of capacity magnitudes in
exact arithmetic.

Writing A for actual augmentations, the implementation costs
O((A+1)(V+E)) for full array initialization and BFS, plus path work
O(AV). Ordinary storage is O(V+E). The usual bound can be written
O(V+E+VE²), including the initial/final search for empty graphs.
To account for many isolated vertices, charge augmentations using W
incident vertices: A=O(WE), with W<=min(V,2E) when a path exists.
Then both terms WE·V and WE² are bounded by O(VE²). Trace copying
adds its explicitly counted history cost. These bounds do not make
checked double arithmetic an exact-real solver.

> Preserve the original CLRS network and both witnesses

The original six-vertex network has ten directed input edges. Its known
maximum flow is 23. The returned source side is S={0,1,2,4}; its
crossing inputs are e4 (1→3, capacity 12), e7 (4→3, capacity 7)
and e9 (4→5, capacity 4). Their sum is 23. The program prints every
per-edge flow, all actual path lengths/bottlenecks, and the independent
numerical certificate. No observational dataset is needed for these
network invariants; explicit graphs permit exact hand checks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/edmonds_karp_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::FlowNetwork g{6,{{0,1,16},{0,2,13},{1,2,10},{2,1,4},{1,3,12},{3,2,9},{2,4,14},{4,3,7},{3,5,20},{4,5,4}},0,5};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::edmonds_karp_trace(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink);
  const auto c=dm::algorithms::max_flow_certificate(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink,t.result);
  if(t.result.max_flow!=23||!c.feasible||!c.optimal_within_tolerance)throw std::runtime_error("original CLRS certificate failed");
  std::print("Original CLRS: flow {}; cut capacity {}; feasible {}; optimal with zero tolerance {}; gap {}.\n",t.result.max_flow,c.cut_capacity,c.feasible,c.optimal_within_tolerance,c.duality_gap);
  std::print("Source side:");for(auto v:t.result.min_cut_source_side)std::print(" {}",v);std::print("; crossing input edges:");for(auto e:c.crossing_edges)std::print(" e{}",e);std::print(".\n\n");
  std::print("| input edge | from | to | capacity | actual flow |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t e=0;e<g.edges.size();++e){const auto [u,v,capacity]=g.edges[e];std::print("| e{} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",e,u,v,capacity,t.result.edge_flow[e]);}
  std::print("\n| BFS | sink distance (V means unreachable) | inspections | flow before | push amount |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t k=0;k<t.searches.size();++k)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,t.searches[k].levels[g.sink],t.searches[k].bfs_arc_inspections,t.searches[k].flow_before,k<t.augmentations.size()?t.augmentations[k].amount:0.);
  std::print("\nWork: {} searches; {} augmentations; {} adjacency inspections; {} path updates; {} captured entries.\n",t.work.bfs_calls,t.work.augmentations,t.work.bfs_arc_inspections,t.work.path_arc_updates,t.captured_entries);
  auto d=dm::algorithms::plot_max_flow(g,t.result,{{0,0},{5,3},{5,-3},{11,3},{11,-3},{16,0}});
  d.text({8,5},"Original CLRS network: matching flow and cut of 23",25).text({8,-5},"Input edge: flow/capacity; red edges cross S to its complement",20).save_svg("build/edmonds_karp_original.svg");
}
