The independent cut certificate uses the supplied input/result; it does
not rerun Edmonds–Karp or choose a more favourable cut. Here integer
capacities and small exact sums give zero capacity/conservation/value
errors and zero gap. More general double inputs still need the reported
errors and explicit tolerance. Four-significant-digit diagram labels
are a display convention; the printed result values remain available.

> Check an exact repeated-search family

For k parallel source-to-sink edges of unit capacity, every path has
one edge and exactly one edge saturates per push. Hence A=k and
there are k+1 complete BFS calls. Each successful BFS reaches both
vertices and inspects all 2k residual adjacency entries. The final
failed BFS inspects the source's k entries, giving

\[
I_{EK}=2k²+k,\qquad L=k.
\]

Dinic instead sends all k units in one blocking phase. It still performs
k path pushes, but needs only two BFS calls and 3k BFS inspections.
This compares these logical searches on one controlled family, not
wall-clock performance or a universal speed ranking. Scaling capacities
by a positive power of two changes the flow values but not these counts.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/edmonds_karp_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<double>x,ek_inspections,dinic_inspections,ek_searches,dinic_searches;
  std::print("| parallel edges k | EK pushes | EK BFS | EK inspections | Dinic pushes | Dinic BFS | Dinic inspections | EK capture |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t k:{1,2,4,8,16,32,64}){const auto g=dm::algorithms::dinic_disjoint_paths(k,1);
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::edmonds_karp_trace(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink);const auto b=dm::algorithms::dinic_max_flow_trace(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink);
    if(a.result.max_flow!=k||b.result.max_flow!=k||a.work.augmentations!=k||a.work.bfs_calls!=k+1||a.work.bfs_arc_inspections!=2*k*k+k||a.work.path_arc_updates!=k||a.captured_entries!=8*k+6||b.work.augmentations!=k||b.work.blocking_phases!=1||b.work.bfs_calls!=2||b.work.bfs_arc_inspections!=3*k)throw std::runtime_error("parallel family identity failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,a.work.augmentations,a.work.bfs_calls,a.work.bfs_arc_inspections,b.work.augmentations,b.work.bfs_calls,b.work.bfs_arc_inspections,a.captured_entries);
    x.push_back(std::log2(k));ek_inspections.push_back(std::log2(a.work.bfs_arc_inspections));dinic_inspections.push_back(std::log2(b.work.bfs_arc_inspections));ek_searches.push_back(a.work.bfs_calls);dinic_searches.push_back(b.work.bfs_calls);}
  std::print("\n| common capacity, k=8 | flow | pushes | inspections |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(double capacity:{.125,1.,8.,1024.}){const auto g=dm::algorithms::dinic_disjoint_paths(8,1,capacity);const auto r=dm::algorithms::edmonds_karp_work(g.vertex_count,g.edges,g.source,g.sink);
    if(r.result.max_flow!=8*capacity||r.work.augmentations!=8||r.work.bfs_arc_inspections!=136)throw std::runtime_error("capacity scale identity failed");std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",capacity,r.result.max_flow,r.work.augmentations,r.work.bfs_arc_inspections);}
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(x,ek_inspections,"Edmonds-Karp",{220,38,38}).points(x,ek_inspections,"",{220,38,38},5).line(x,dinic_inspections,"Dinic",{37,99,235}).points(x,dinic_inspections,"",{37,99,235},5).title("Quadratic versus linear BFS inspections").x_label("log2(parallel edges k)").y_label("log2(residual arc inspections)").y_limits(0,16);
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(x,ek_searches,"Edmonds-Karp",{220,38,38}).line(x,dinic_searches,"Dinic",{37,99,235}).title("Repeated BFS versus one blocking phase").x_label("log2(parallel edges k)").y_label("Complete BFS calls").y_limits(0,78);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,520).title("Same k path pushes; different numbers of shortest-path searches").fit_panels().save_svg("build/edmonds_karp_work.svg");
}
